%% Figure 3: Core Business Sequence Diagram -- Full Wrong-Answer Trap Diagnosis Flow (Sequence Diagram: Diagnose)
%% JC2001 Group 5 / StudyGraph Smart Study Assistant
%% Notes:
%%   1. Participants and core contracts align with the current FastAPI modular service architecture: POST /api/diagnose
%%      (receives question_id and selected_option); optional planned extension POST /api/tutor.
%%   2. The alt branches in the figure are NFR-02 "offline reliability": the external graph and external model are both optional;
%%      when either is unavailable the core flow still returns results from local curated content.
%%   3. Label [Implemented] = already landed in backend/app and frontend/app.js and covered by tests;
%%      [Planned] = design goal, not yet wired to a real external service; [Optional] = injected via environment variable.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as University Student
    participant UI as Frontend Console (app.js)
    participant API as Business Hub (backend/app)
    participant Store as Question Bank and Knowledge Base (seed_questions.py)
    participant Graph as Neo4j Graph (cloud)
    participant Qwen as Qwen-Turbo

    User->>UI: Clicks a distractor option (e.g. option B)
    UI->>API: POST /api/diagnose {question_id, selected_option}
    API->>Store: Read question stem, standard answer and trap mappings [Implemented]
    Store-->>API: trap_id, misconception, prerequisite
    Note over API,Store: Answers and misconception mappings are not exposed by the public question API
    API->>API: evaluate_answer sets is_correct=false
    alt External graph available [Planned]
        API->>Graph: MATCH (q:Question)-[:PRONE_TO]->(t:Trap)
        Graph-->>API: Topic names, predecessor concepts and trigger labels
    else Graph miss or timeout [degraded]
        API->>API: Fall back to the local curated misconception topology and prerequisite knowledge
    end
    API-->>UI: 200 OK (DiagnoseResponse: {is_correct, trap, socratic_hint, prerequisite, radar_updates})
    UI->>UI: Expand the right-hand diagnosis drawer and highlight the option
    UI-->>User: Show Socratic guidance, prerequisite concepts and pitfall-avoidance advice
    opt Student continues with follow-up rounds [Planned · tutor follow-up extension]
        User->>UI: Types a follow-up into the chat drawer
        UI->>API: POST /api/tutor {question_id, message}
        alt External model configured [Optional]
            API->>Qwen: Compatible-protocol request /chat/completions
            Qwen-->>API: Returns a deeper heuristic follow-up reply
        else Model not configured or call timed out [local fallback]
            API->>API: local_tutor_reply generated from the reviewed evidence chain
        end
        API-->>UI: 200 OK {reply, mode}
        UI-->>User: Show the tutor reply with source annotations
    end
    UI->>UI: Append the answer record to localStorage
    UI-->>User: Refresh the mastery radar and dimension pass status
